  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">YCC (SCOPE-PFM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">YCC&#x2019;s mission to empower youth, strengthen democratic governance, and promote a more transparent and accountable Cambodia, is aligned with the SCOPE-PFM project. It benefits both the organization and the wider population by fostering inclusive civic participationand encouraging responsible public spending.

Although youth make up a large share of Cambodia&#x2019;s population, they continue to face systemic barriers that limit their involvement in governance and policymaking. This project helps address those challenges by equipping young people&#x2014;especially high school students and youth leaders&#x2014;with the knowledge, skills, and platforms needed to meaningfully engage in public financial management (PFM). Through targeted training, structured dialogues, and community-based campaigns, youth will learn about budget transparency and gender-responsive public services, while also becoming active contributors to local development processes.

For YCC, this project serves as a catalyst for transformation. It strengthens our grassroots networks, deepens partnerships with local authorities and civil society, and reinforces our role as a key advocate for youth-led democratic reform. The project also builds on YCC&#x2019;s previous successes, including initiatives like ISAC, enabling the organization to scale its impact and introduce innovative approaches.

Moreover, the project directly supports YCC&#x2019;s strategic objectives in education, governance, and environmental sustainability. It allows YCC to bring youth voices into budgeting processes that influence education, natural resource management, and social protection&#x2014;areas critical to Cambodia&#x2019;s future. Ultimately, this project is a timely and powerful extension of YCC&#x2019;s vision: to cultivate a generation of informed, confident,and engaged youth who can help shape a more transparent, accountable,and democratic Cambodia.</narrative>
  </description>
